{
  "title": "Cellato: A C++20 Library and Embedded DSL for Cellular Automata",
  "description": "<p>Cellato is a high-performance C++20 library and embedded domain-specific language (DSL) for cellular automata. It lets users describe cellular automaton rules as type-level C++ expressions and execute them across multiple evaluators, memory layouts (standard cells, bit arrays, bit planes, tiled bit planes), and traversers (CPU, CUDA, spatial blocking, temporal blocking).</p>",
